{"cuisine/chinese-imperial-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/chinese-imperial-cuisine","n":"Chinese imperial cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Beijing cuisine","cuisine/beijing-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in China","intro":[["Chinese imperial cuisine is derived from a variety of cooking styles of the regions in China, mainly from the cuisines of Shandong and Jiangsu provinces. The style originated from various Emperors' Kitchen and the Empress Dowagers' Kitchen, and it is similar to Beijing cuisine which it heavily influenced."],["Imperial cuisine was served mainly to the emperors, their empresses and concubines, and the imperial family. The characteristics of the Chinese imperial cuisine are the elaborate cooking methods and the strict selection of raw materials, which are often extremely expensive, rare or complicated in preparation. Visual presentation is also very important, so the colour and the shape of the dish must be carefully arranged. The most famous Chinese imperial cuisine restaurants are both located in Beijing: Fang Shan in Beihai Park and Ting Li Ting (聽鸝廳; tīng lí tīng) in the Summer Palace."],["Styles and tastes of Chinese imperial cuisine vary from dynasty to dynasty. Every dynasty has its own distinguishing features. The two famous styles of Chinese imperial cuisine are from the Ming and Qing dynasties. Many famous dishes emerged in these dynasties, such as Wensi tofu and Peking duck."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"chinese-imperial-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_imperial_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Beijing cuisine","cuisine/beijing-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Food for the Emperor: Recipes of Imperial China with a Dictionary of Chinese Cuisine","ref":"cookbook/food-for-the-emperor-recipes-of-imperial-china-with-a-dictionary-of-chinese-cuisine","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"John D. Keys","note":"Older English collection of recipes associated with the imperial kitchens, with a glossary of Chinese culinary terms.","url":"","suggested":true}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Beijing cuisine","cuisine/beijing-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/5e/Manchu_Han_Imperial_Feast_Tao_Heung_Museum_of_Food_Culture.jpg/500px-Manchu_Han_Imperial_Feast_Tao_Heung_Museum_of_Food_Culture.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Cara Chow (Charlotte1125)","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manchu_Han_Imperial_Feast_Tao_Heung_Museum_of_Food_Culture.jpg"}},"cuisine/shanxi-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/shanxi-cuisine","n":"Shanxi cuisine","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Asia","cuisines#asia"],["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in China","intro":[["Shanxi cuisine, or Jin cuisine, is derived from the native cooking styles of Shanxi Province in China. Local dishes include noodles, fried flatbread (da bing), and vinegar. Sour tastes are typical."],["Shanxi cuisine is not well known outside the region, partially due to its lower population compared to other provinces."],["Pork, chicken and lamb are among the most common meats—goat, and sheep offal are also often used. For example, lamb soup is usually cooked with livers, stomach and other offal. Lamb is used in Shanxi in ways that combines the cuisines of Northern Chinese minorities and Han Chinese. For example, using ground lamb and carrots as a dumpling filling, is something that is not found in any other Chinese cooking styles. Ground pork with chopped dill is another popular dumpling filling."],["The main staples reflect the crops commonly grown in Shanxi: millet, sorghum, and wheat. Pork, mushrooms, potatoes and turnips are frequently used."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"shanxi-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanxi_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Asian cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/16/Datong_Fideos.jpg/500px-Datong_Fideos.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Seba Della y Sole Bossio from Cordoba, Argentina","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Datong_Fideos.jpg"}},"dish/alex-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/alex-restaurant","n":"Alex (restaurant)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Alex was a French restaurant located in Las Vegas, Nevada, United States, that held two Michelin stars. It is the namesake restaurant of celebrity chef Alessandro Stratta, Iron Chef USA, and winner of the James Beard Foundation Award for \"Best Chef Southwest\" in 1998. The restaurant was well known for Stratta's unique approach and attention to molecular gastronomy. The restaurant was considered one of the finest in the United States. It closed indefinitely on January 15, 2011."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-alex-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alex_(restaurant)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","ref":"site/pardonyourfrench-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","ref":"site/lacuisinedegeraldine-fr","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","ref":"site/newcaledonia-travel","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"https://www.newcaledonia.travel/nz/gastronomy-wine/gastronomy/kanak-cooking","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from French cuisine","links":[["'t Fornuis","dish/t-fornuis"],["'t Misverstant","dish/t-misverstant"],["'t Vlasbloemeken","dish/t-vlasbloemeken"],["&moshik","dish/moshik"],["Aan de Poel","dish/aan-de-poel"],["Adrian (restaurant)","dish/adrian-restaurant"],["Adventureland Bazaar","dish/adventureland-bazaar"],["Alain Ducasse at The Dorchester","dish/alain-ducasse-at-the-dorchester"],["Albufera sauce","dish/albufera-sauce"],["Andouillette","dish/andouillette"],["Arpège (restaurant)","dish/arpege-restaurant"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Atelier Crenn","dish/atelier-crenn"],["Au Coin des Bons Enfants","dish/au-coin-des-bons-enfants"],["Au Crocodile","dish/au-crocodile"],["Au Pied de Cochon (Mexico City)","dish/au-pied-de-cochon-mexico-city"],["Auberge (restaurant)","dish/auberge-restaurant"],["Auberge De Kieviet","dish/auberge-de-kieviet"],["Aubergine (London restaurant)","dish/aubergine-london-restaurant"],["Auguste (restaurant)","dish/auguste-restaurant"],["Bagatelle (restaurant)","dish/bagatelle-restaurant"],["Balthazar (restaurant)","dish/balthazar-restaurant"],["Bardot Brasserie","dish/bardot-brasserie"],["Bâtard (restaurant)","dish/batard-restaurant"],["Baumé (restaurant)","dish/baume-restaurant"],["Bayonne ham","dish/bayonne-ham"],["Be Our Guest Restaurant","dish/be-our-guest-restaurant"],["Beaulieu, Doorwerth Castle","dish/beaulieu-doorwerth-castle"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Bell's (restaurant)","dish/bell-s-restaurant"],["Belmond Le Manoir aux Quat'Saisons","dish/belmond-le-manoir-aux-quat-saisons"],["Beluga (restaurant)","dish/beluga-restaurant"],["Berowra Waters Inn","dish/berowra-waters-inn"],["Beurre maître d'hôtel","dish/beurre-maitre-d-hotel"],["Beurre manié","dish/beurre-manie"],["Bisque (food)","dish/bisque-food"],["Bistro 990","dish/bistro-990"],["Bistro Agnes","dish/bistro-agnes"],["Bistro Jeanty","dish/bistro-jeanty"],["Bistro Moulin","dish/bistro-moulin"]]}]},"dish/algerienne-sauce":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/algerienne-sauce","n":"Algérienne sauce","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Belgian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Algérienne sauce or Algerian sauce is a sweet and spicy sauce with a yellowish-orange color. It is often available at fast-food businesses serving French tacos or kebabs, as well as friteries and other similar fast-food businesses, in Algeria, Tunisia, Morocco, Belgium, France, Switzerland, Japan and Québec."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-algerienne-sauce"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alg%C3%A9rienne_sauce"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Belgian cuisine","cuisine/belgian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Harissa","ingredient/harissa"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"]]},{"h":"More from Belgian cuisine","links":[["'t Fornuis","dish/t-fornuis"],["Belgian chocolate","dish/belgian-chocolate"],["Belgo","dish/belgo"],["Bickyburger","dish/bickyburger"],["Boûkète","dish/boukete"],["Flemish stew","dish/flemish-stew"],["Friterie","dish/friterie"],["Hertog Jan (restaurant)","dish/hertog-jan-restaurant"],["Hof van Cleve","dish/hof-van-cleve"],["Liège waffle","dish/liege-waffle"],["Moules-frites","dish/moules-frites"],["Paling in 't groen","dish/paling-in-t-groen"],["Samurai sauce","dish/samurai-sauce"],["Speculoos","dish/speculoos"],["Steak tartare","dish/steak-tartare"],["Waterzooi","dish/waterzooi"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/72/Alg%C3%A9rienne_sauce_from_O%27Tacos.jpg/500px-Alg%C3%A9rienne_sauce_from_O%27Tacos.jpg","w":500,"h":500,"by":"The wub","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alg%C3%A9rienne_sauce_from_O'Tacos.jpg"}},"dish/butter-chicken":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/butter-chicken","n":"Butter chicken","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Butter chicken or murgh makhani is a curry made from chicken cooked in a spiced tomato and butter-based (makhani) gravy. The gravy is known for its creamy, rich texture. It is similar to chicken tikka masala, which uses a tomato paste. The dish was invented by Indian chefs Kundan Lal Gujral and Kundan Lal Jaggi and is associated with their Moti Mahal restaurant in Daryaganj, Delhi which popularized it in the 1950s. It has since become a staple cuisine of the city."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-butter-chicken"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butter_chicken"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Garam masala","ingredient/garam-masala"],["Kasuri methi","ingredient/kasuri-methi"],["Tomatoes","ingredient/tomatoes"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Swasthi's Recipes","ref":"site/indianhealthyrecipes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"indianhealthyrecipes.com","note":"Swasthi Shreekanth's long-running blog of everyday Indian home cooking from across the regions.","url":"https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/about/","suggested":true},{"name":"Hari Ghotra","ref":"site/harighotra-co-uk","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"harighotra.co.uk","note":"UK-based cook Hari Ghotra's recipe library and videos of home-style Indian dishes.","url":"https://www.harighotra.co.uk/indian-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Indian cuisine","links":[["Akuri","dish/akuri"],["Aloo paratha","dish/aloo-paratha"],["Amba (condiment)","dish/amba-condiment"],["Annapurna Cafe","dish/annapurna-cafe"],["Baingan bharta","dish/baingan-bharta"],["Bombay potato","dish/bombay-potato"],["Chaat masala","dish/chaat-masala"],["Chai Pani","dish/chai-pani"],["Chicken Chettinad","dish/chicken-chettinad"],["Chutney Mary","dish/chutney-mary"],["Dahi vada","dish/dahi-vada"],["Dal dhokli","dish/dal-dhokli"],["Dal makhani","dish/dal-makhani"],["Dhamaka (restaurant)","dish/dhamaka-restaurant"],["East India Co. Grill and Bar","dish/east-india-co-grill-and-bar"],["Fafda","dish/fafda"],["Falooda","dish/falooda"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Gaggan","dish/gaggan"],["Handvo","dish/handvo"],["Hindoostane Coffee House","dish/hindoostane-coffee-house"],["Hyderabadi haleem","dish/hyderabadi-haleem"],["Idli","dish/idli"],["Indian restaurant","dish/indian-restaurant"],["Kachumber","dish/kachumber"],["Kidyo","dish/kidyo"],["Kulfi","dish/kulfi"],["Lasan","dish/lasan"],["Maruti Indian Restaurant","dish/maruti-indian-restaurant"],["Masala chai","dish/masala-chai"],["Masala y Maíz","dish/masala-y-maiz"],["Mirchi bada","dish/mirchi-bada"],["Mokthuk","dish/mokthuk"],["Naan","dish/naan"],["Osmania biscuit","dish/osmania-biscuit"],["Panipuri","dish/panipuri"],["Pathia","dish/pathia"],["Rabri","dish/rabri"],["Semma (restaurant)","dish/semma-restaurant"],["Shemai","dish/shemai"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/3c/Chicken_makhani.jpg/500px-Chicken_makhani.jpg","w":500,"h":332,"by":"stu_spivack","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chicken_makhani.jpg"}},"dish/cabalen":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/cabalen","n":"Cabalen","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Kapampangan cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Cabalen is a Philippine buffet restaurant chain primarily serving traditional Filipino entrees heavy on influences from the Pampanga region of Central Luzon, as well as dishes from Filipino, Thai, and Japanese cuisines. However, most of the meals are from Kapampangan cuisine. Most of the chain's restaurants are located in Metro Manila, with one restaurant located in Cebu province and a single unit in the United States. Some of the locations are franchised operations. Many locations are situated within shopping malls."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-cabalen"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabalen"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Kapampangan cuisine","cuisine/kapampangan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Kapampangan Kitchen","ref":"site/kapampangankitchen-blogspot-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kapampangankitchen.blogspot.com","note":"Blog dedicated to Kapampangan home recipes from Pampanga.","url":"https://kapampangankitchen.blogspot.com","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Kapampangan cuisine","links":[["Tibok-tibok","dish/tibok-tibok"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/27/Cabalenphil.jpg/500px-Cabalenphil.jpg","w":500,"h":322,"by":"96ersoftexas","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cabalenphil.jpg"}},"dish/dongpo-pork":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dongpo-pork","n":"Dongpo pork","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Dongpo pork, also known as Dongpo meat, is a Hangzhou dish made by pan-frying and then red-cooking pork belly. The pork is typically cut into thick, approximately five-centimetre (two-inch) squares, with an even distribution of fat and lean meat, whilst retaining the skin. The texture is tender and juicy without being excessively greasy, accompanied by a fragrant aroma of wine. The dish is named in honor of Su Dongpo (Su Shi), a distinguished Song Dynasty poet and gastronome."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dongpo-pork"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dongpo_pork"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Pork belly","ingredient/pork-belly"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","ref":"site/thewoksoflife-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","ref":"site/youtube-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cooking.","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ChineseCookingDemystified","suggested":true},{"name":"Red House Spice","ref":"site/redhousespice-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"redhousespice.com","note":"Classic Chinese recipes from Wei Guo, who grew up in Gansu, blogging since 2017.","url":"https://redhousespice.com/about/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Chinese cuisine","links":[["A+ Hong Kong Kitchen","dish/a-hong-kong-kitchen"],["Almond biscuit","dish/almond-biscuit"],["Banana roll","dish/banana-roll"],["Baozi","dish/baozi"],["Bear paw","dish/bear-paw"],["Black sesame roll","dish/black-sesame-roll"],["Century egg","dish/century-egg"],["Cha siu bao","dish/cha-siu-bao"],["Chinese restaurant","dish/chinese-restaurant"],["Chinese Tuxedo","dish/chinese-tuxedo"],["Chowking","dish/chowking"],["Classic Savory","dish/classic-savory"],["Country Dough","dish/country-dough"],["Cuisine AuntDai","dish/cuisine-auntdai"],["Dandan noodles","dish/dandan-noodles"],["Dapanji","dish/dapanji"],["Dim Sum King","dish/dim-sum-king"],["Dong'an chicken","dish/dong-an-chicken"],["Donkey burger","dish/donkey-burger"],["Doujiang","dish/doujiang"],["Drunken shrimp","dish/drunken-shrimp"],["Duck House Chinese Restaurant","dish/duck-house-chinese-restaurant"],["Edible bird's nest","dish/edi